ExperienceDocument
  kind: Kind.CIRCUIT
  title: "2N2222 as a switch"
  slug: "bjt-switch"
  type: Optional.empty
  meta: Meta
      summary: "A 2N2222A switching a 100 Ω load from 12 V, its base driven by a square wave. At 1 kΩ it saturates: the collector swings between 12 V and 0.1 V. Turn the base resistor past about 7 kΩ and it leaves saturation — the collector stops reaching the bottom and the transistor warms."
